{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 128, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 5 empty, removing edge 3 leaves node 3 fed only by edge 4, so the cell loses paths into the output and risks disconnection."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When the direct input-to-output edge is already missing, removing edge 5 starves the output node of paths."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "If edge 0 is none, node 1 is dead and edge 4 carries nothing, so removing it costs little."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 4 absent, node 1 only feeds edge 2, so cutting edge 0 removes less useful computation."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-to-output edge with a conv adds capacity, whereas replacing an existing skip or pool loses a useful shortcut."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where there was no edge opens a new path to the output instead of swapping one operation for another."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual shortcut to a cell that lacks one improves optimisation more than replacing an existing parametric op."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 1 is none, edge 2 is node 2's only input, so removing it kills node 2 and edge 5's contribution."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "A conv on edge 4 is useless when node 1 i